{"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Choosing Destinations","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Deliver events to your logs, your traces, a server or memory, and decide what each destination may see.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"],"generated":true,"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"Destination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a plain sink: "},{"code":"deliver(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hands it each batch of records. Traffluent ships a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"few, each in a module of its own, so an app links only the ones it uses."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Logs and traces","anchor":"Logs-and-traces","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To see events beside your logs or traces, deliver to ","type":"text"},{"code":"LoggerDestination(logger:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations"},{"text":") or ","type":"text"},{"code":"SpanEventDestination(tracer:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Only apps that use swift-log or swift-distributed-tracing this way link them. A span event joins","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the span that was active when the event was tracked, even if delivery runs later.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"A server","anchor":"A-server","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send batches to a server, deliver to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination(endpoint:headerFields:encoder:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). It posts each batch as one request whose body is what your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes for it, so events need no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance and the wire format is yours. It sends with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" by default, or through any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" you pass as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport:"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after a wait, until it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"answered with 2xx. The waits start at 1 second and double up to 60 seconds; pass an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff:"},{"text":" for others, and a test clock as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock:"},{"text":" in tests. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one arrives, so a tracker’s store keeps its records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until then, and a batch still being retried when the app ends is sent again on the next launch.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Other destinations aren’t held up. Meanwhile the delivery’s later batches wait in this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination’s buffer of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batchBufferLimit"},{"text":" batches, which drops its oldest when full; a store keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the records of a dropped batch for the next launch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some batches won’t succeed if sent again, so they are dropped: one the endpoint answers with any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other status, one whose request the transport can never send (a malformed URL, a scheme it doesn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"support, or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http"},{"type":"text","text":" URL that App Transport Security refuses), and one the encoder can’t encode."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The destination logs each at error level and reports it on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":", with the records’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifiers and the status, the transport’s reason or the encoder’s error. Cancelling the delivery"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stops the retries."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bootstrapped tracing instrument, or the one you pass as "},{"code":"instrument:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", injects the trace"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context of the batch’s first record into the request’s header fields, so a server that extracts it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"joins the request to the app’s trace. The encoder’s "},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" always wins, and with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instrument bootstrapped no header is added. Only the first record’s context travels in the header"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields; write each record’s context into the body if the server needs it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to a self-hosted TraffluentCollector, give ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder(plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding"},{"text":") as its encoder, and the collector’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API key as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization: Bearer"},{"text":" header field. It writes the collector’s ingest format: each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record’s identifier (which a redelivered record keeps), its name, timestamp and redelivery marker,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its properties read through the event’s schema in your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":", and its standard context and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trace context. A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is sent only while the record reveals it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the rest of its batch is sent.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"That happens when the plan has no schema for the record’s event at its version (an event the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library tracks, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionStarted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", that the plan doesn’t list), when the event isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryCodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or when a value has no JSON form, such as a NaN. The encoder logs each skipped","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record at error level, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s. A batch with no record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the encoder can write sends nothing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Memory","anchor":"Memory","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To read what was tracked inside the app, deliver to an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"text":" as well (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","type":"reference"},{"text":"): for an event inspector in a debug build, a recent-activity view, a SwiftUI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preview, or a test of what your code tracks. It keeps the newest 1,000 records, or as many as you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity:"},{"text":", dropping the oldest across batches; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination.unbounded()"},{"text":" keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every one. Read it with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events(of: SignedUp.self)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"records"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batches"},{"text":", or wait on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliveries"},{"text":", which announces each batch to one reader.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Sensitive values and call sites","anchor":"Sensitive-values-and-call-sites","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A property that destinations shouldn’t see unless they must is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value. A destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads it only through the record, with ","type":"text"},{"code":"reveal(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and printing or mirroring it shows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"<redacted>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" makes a destination’s records reveal nothing, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"droppingCallSite()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removes their call sites. Every other destination receives both:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct SignedIn: Event {","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}","","let backend = InMemoryDestination()","let vendor = InMemoryDestination()","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(","    to: backend,","    vendor.redactingSensitiveValues().droppingCallSite()",")","tracker.track(SignedIn(email: Sensitive(\"ada@example.com\")))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()","let event = backend.events(of: SignedIn.self)[0]","let email = backend.records[0].reveal(event.email)    \/\/ \"ada@example.com\"","let redacted = vendor.records[0].reveal(event.email)  \/\/ nil","let callSite = vendor.records[0].sourceLocation       \/\/ nil"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"accepting(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" narrows a destination to the consent categories it serves (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Traffluent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"HTTPDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","type":"topic"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"kind":"symbol","title":"TracingDestinations","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"Destinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","url":"\/documentation\/destinations","type":"topic"},"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding":{"kind":"symbol","title":"CollectorEncoding","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/collectorencoding","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://LoggingDestinations/documentation/LoggingDestinations":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"LoggingDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/loggingdestinations","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"abstract":[{"text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","title":"Consent Gating","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TestingWhatYouTrack":{"kind":"article","title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingFromViews":{"kind":"article","title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give views the tracker the way each framework passes values down, and let modifiers and controls track what views do."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingEvents":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track typed events with a tracker, then deliver them in batches to any number of destinations."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Tracking Events","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingevents","type":"topic"}}}